5. Simple 'end to end' test system, for improved dev confidence when iterating
   Modeled on my manual 'test flow':
    - For a clankerized repo
        - the app should start, display UI
        - all domain buttons should
            - if inhabitet, display proper msg
            - if unhabited, display proper msg
        - then, for each domain button, every prompt button should
            - if prompt button inhabitet, produce a prompt of expected size
            - if no inhabitant, display appropriate msg
        - for any and all buttons outside the keys specified by system_cfg
            - be silently ignored, and not cause crash as they do now
            - exception for things like esc, ctrl+c, ctrl+d and other 'system keys'
    - When clankerizing a repo:
        - it should produce a repo on the expected format, containing all members of a yet to be declared 'repo contract'
        - then it should pass the 'clankerized repo' test
        - perhaps also a 'unruly repo' scenario, where the repo already contains things contract mandates
            - > than complain to user, do no harm
        - so clankerization must be safe. Perhaps the confirm msg can first check and see that it is so? else complain to user 

10. clankerization of a project can represent the much talked about repo contract by the content it creates
